ith BugBot and Background Agent\",\n    \"description\": \"Cursor 1.0 release featuring BugBot for automatic code review, Background Agent access for all users, Jupyter Notebook support, Memories feature, MCP one-click install, OAuth support, and richer chat responses with visualizations.\",\n    \"updateType\": \"major_release\",\n    \"url\": \"https://cursor.sh/changelog\",\n    \"date\": \"2026-04-20\",\n    \"community_feedback\": []\n  },\n  {\n    \"productName\": \"Cursor\",\n    \"title\": \"Background Agents in Slack Integration\",\n    \"description\": \"You can now launch Background Agents directly from Slack by mentioning @Cursor. Agents can read the thread, understand context, and create PRs in GitHub without leaving the conversation.\",\n    \"updateType\": \"new_feature\",\n    \"url\": \"https://cursor.sh/changelog\",\n    \"date\": \"2026-04-28\",\n    \"community_feedback\": []\n  },\n  {\n    \"productName\": \"Continue\",\n    \"title\": \"Check on Your Spaghetti Software Factory\",\n    \"description\": \"Blog post discussing quality control in AI-assisted development, emphasizing that everyone building with AI agents is speedrunning the Factorio experience and that slop compounds - the fix is systematic quality control, not faster review.\",\n    \"updateType\": \"blog_post\",\n    \"url\": \"https://continue.dev/blog\",\n    \"date\": \"2026-03-06\",\n    \"community_feedback\": []\n  }\n]\n"
